From 2fa325b896e6d7d12bf353661575911c52fc920c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ayushman Bhattacharya <ayushman.elixpo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:30:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] avformat: add RV565 demuxer and muxer

A little-endian header ("RV5", version, width, height, frame rate,
flags, frame count; version 7 adds the header size, pixel format, codec
and keyframe interval) followed by one length-prefixed record per frame.
The demuxer reads versions 6 and 7. Version 6 records lack the frame
type byte, so the demuxer adds one and both versions give the same
packets.

On seekable input the demuxer validates every record when the file is
opened (empty or truncated records, unknown frame types, a missing
keyframe at a multiple of the keyframe interval, repeats with a body,
stored bodies of the wrong size, bytes after the last record), as the
specification requires, and indexes keyframes so a seek lands on the
keyframe at or before the target, at most interval - 1 records away.
Streamed input is checked record by record. Byte seeking is rejected.

The muxer writes version 7, or version 6 with -format_version 6 for
older players, checks records against the same rules, and patches the
frame count at the end.

FATE: libavformat/tests/rv565 covers validation of seekable and
streamed input and keyframe seeking; fate-rv565-enc-* encode a clip with
repeated frames to every pixel format with stored frames, plus zlib with
deltas and version 6 output; fate-lavf-rv565 and fate-seek-lavf-rv565
round-trip the lavf test clip; and fate-rv565-* decode conformance
vectors from the specification (samples: rv565/).

Specification: https://github.com/elixpo/rv565/blob/main/docs/FORMAT.md

Signed-off-by: Ayushman Bhattacharya <ayushman.elixpo@gmail.com>
